<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thagaste</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thagaste was a Roman town in Numidia, on the site of modern Souk Ahras in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. It is best known as the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augustine-of-hippo">Augustine of Hippo</a> in 354, who returned there after his conversion to found a religious community before becoming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Hippo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thagaste.jpg" alt="Thagaste" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heinrich Kiepert · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mileve_Hippo_Thagaste_in_Numidia_(83193756).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
